psyq-wasm is distributed under two licenses, applied per file. Every source
file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier header naming its license.

SPDX expression for the package as a whole: MIT AND GPL-2.0-only

1. MIT (LICENSES/MIT.txt)

   Original work in this repository:

   - the TypeScript wrapper (src/) and its compiled output (dist/*.js,
     dist/*.d.ts, except dist/cc1psx.js, dist/cc1psx.wasm, dist/cccp.js, and
     dist/cccp.wasm);
   - build scripts and configuration (build/*.sh, build/pins.env,
     build/objs.txt, build/cccp-objs.txt, package files, CI workflows);
   - tests, test fixtures, and helpers (test/), the demo (demo/), and
     documentation.

2. GPL-2.0-only (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt)

   Work derived from the GNU C Compiler 2.8.1 as modified for the Sony PsyQ
   toolchain, which is licensed under the GNU General Public License,
   version 2:

   - build/gen/        generated GCC sources (parser tables, insn-* files,
                       configuration headers) produced by the historical
                       build described in PROVENANCE.md;
   - build/patches/    compatibility patches applied to the GCC sources;
   - dist/cc1psx.wasm  the compiled compiler;
   - dist/cc1psx.js    the Emscripten glue that loads it (Emscripten's own
                       runtime portions are MIT / Apache-2.0 with LLVM
                       exception; the combined file is distributed under
                       GPL-2.0-only);
   - dist/cccp.wasm    the compiled GCC 2.8.1 preprocessor, built from the
                       same sources;
   - dist/cccp.js      its Emscripten glue, under the same terms as
                       dist/cc1psx.js.

   The complete corresponding source for the compiler artifact is identified
   in PROVENANCE.md and published with every release as a source archive.

No original proprietary Sony binaries are included in this repository or in
the published package.
